course: dictionary
lesson: 13141
title: The forefinger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your forefinger is the finger next to your thumb. It is the one you usually use to point. «She pointed at the door with her forefinger.» Here, the word tells you which finger she used.
explain: The forefinger is also called the index finger or the first finger. These are other names for the same finger. «Press the button with your forefinger.» If you see index or first finger in a science book, it means the forefinger.
explain: Context clues help here too. «He held the tiny seed between his thumb and forefinger.» The thumb is next to the forefinger, so you can picture where it is. «Mum wagged her forefinger at me» is a clue that she was telling you off.
fact: The forefinger is the finger next to your thumb.
fact: You often use your forefinger to point, press buttons and beckon.
fact: Forefinger is also called the index finger or first finger.
fact: On the hand, the five fingers are thumb, forefinger, middle, ring and little finger (pinkie).
fact: «Between thumb and forefinger» means held between those two fingers, as in «a grain of rice between thumb and forefinger».
exercise: «She pointed at the door with her forefinger.» Which finger did she point with? | The ring finger | The little finger | *The finger next to the thumb | The middle finger
exercise: Ravi says his forefinger is his pinkie. Is he right? | Yes, it is the smallest finger | No, the forefinger is the thumb itself | Yes, it is the finger on your foot | *No, the forefinger is next to the thumb
exercise: Which other name means the same as forefinger? | Thumb | *Index finger | Pinkie | Ring finger
test: «Mum wagged her forefinger at me.» What might this show? | *She was telling me off | She was waving hello | She had hurt her hand | She was very cold
test: On the hand, which finger comes between the thumb and the middle finger? | Little finger | Pinkie | *Forefinger | Ring finger
exam: Which phrase about the forefinger is one of the phrases in the lessons? | *Between thumb and forefinger | Open the door | Eat the cake slowly | Run past the gate
